<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vanand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vanand was a historical district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayrarat">Ayrarat</a>, centred on the fortress town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> in present-day north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. Under the Bagratids it became the seat of a separate Armenian kingdom, the Kingdom of Kars, created in 963 when Ashot III granted it to his brother Mushegh. The kingdom lasted until 1065, when its last king ceded it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vanand.jpg" alt="Vanand" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Soghomon Matevosyan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D5%8E%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%A4_%D4%B1%D5%B5%D6%80%D5%A1%D6%80%D5%A1%D5%BF_%D5%B6%D5%A1%D5%B0%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%A3_page353-2000px-%D5%80%D5%A1%D5%B5%D5%AF%D5%A1%D5%AF%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%8D%D5%B8%D5%BE%D5%A5%D5%BF%D5%A1%D5%AF%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%80%D5%A1%D5%B6%D6%80%D5%A1%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%BF%D5%A1%D6%80%D5%A1%D5%B6_(Soviet_Armenian_Encyclopedia)_1_copy_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
